    "sourceDescription": "Requisition Details & Talent Acquisition Contact REQ ID: 147589 Talent Acquisition Specialist: Lerato Sithole Location: Gauteng Closing Date: 24 November 2026 Job Family Sales and Services Career Stream Client Solutions Leadership Pipeline Manage Managers FAIS Affected FAIS Affected - Yes Why Join Our Team Join a team shaping the future of growth across priority sectors. This is an opportunity to influence sector strategy, unlock meaningful commercial opportunities and mobilise teams across the business to deliver sustainable market share, revenue and portfolio growth. Job Purpose To lead the development and execution of growth strategies across priority sectors, increasing market share, deepening sector penetration and delivering sustainable revenue and portfolio growth. The role is accountable for identifying high-potential opportunities, converting sector insight into commercially viable initiatives and mobilising cross-functional teams to deliver measurable business outcomes. Job Responsibilities Sector Strategy and Thought Leadership Develop and lead commercially focused strategies for priority growth sectors, aligned with the organisation’s broader Business and Commercial Banking objectives. Drive the prioritisation and activation of sector growth opportunities to increase market share, deepen sector penetration and support sustainable portfolio growth . Provide sector thought leadership and market intelligence to guide strategic decision-making, client propositions and investment priorities. Identify emerging market trends, competitive threats and high-potential opportunities across relevant sectors, markets and client segments. Translate sector insights and strategic priorities into executable growth initiatives with clearly defined commercial objectives and performance measures. Work collaboratively with product, sales, client coverage, risk, credit and other relevant stakeholders to deliver integrated sector propositions and measurable commercial outcomes. Monitor the performance of sector growth initiatives and implement corrective action where delivery is below agreed expectations. Maintain sound risk, financial and governance discipline when evaluating and activating sector growth opportunities. Commercial Growth and Execution Deliver measurable improvements in market share, client acquisition, revenue and portfolio growth across priority sectors. Build and maintain a sustainable pipeline of commercially viable sector opportunities. Ensure that growth strategies move beyond sector advisory and strategy development into implementation and measurable commercial delivery. Establish appropriate performance measures and provide transparent reporting on the progress and impact of sector growth initiatives. Drive accountability for sustainable commercial performance while maintaining an appropriate balance between growth, risk and return. People and Stakeholder Leadership Lead, develop and manage the performance of managers or senior commercial teams. Mobilise stakeholders across organisational boundaries to execute sector growth priorities and deliver measurable commercial outcomes. Build effective partnerships across Business and Commercial Banking, product, client coverage, credit, risk, operations and enabling functions. Influence senior stakeholders, resolve trade-offs and establish clear accountability, decision rights and success measures across sector initiatives. Promote a high-performance culture focused on accountability, collaboration, client outcomes and disciplined execution. Job Responsibilities Continue Risk Appetite, Governance and Control Ensure sector growth strategies, activities and recommendations are delivered within approved risk appetite, credit, conduct, compliance, FAIS and regulatory frameworks. Provide input into risk appetite considerations by identifying sector risks, concentration concerns, client suitability factors and emerging market exposures. Balance commercial growth opportunities with appropriate risk, return, portfolio quality and responsible banking considerations. Drive proactive identification and escalation of material risks, control gaps and decision dependencies that could affect sustainable portfolio performance. Maintain appropriate governance discipline, evidence-based decision-making and accountability in the activation and monitoring of sector growth initiatives. Portfolio Insight and Commercial Enablement Monitor portfolio performance, growth indicators, pipeline quality, client penetration and risk-adjusted returns to identify opportunities and areas requiring intervention. Translate sector, portfolio and performance insights into clear commercial priorities and actions. Ensure growth recommendations balance commercial opportunity with pricing discipline, credit quality and sustainable client outcomes. Ideal Candidate A strategic and results-driven leader with strong Business and Commercial Banking experience, credible sector expertise and a proven track record of delivering measurable market share growth, deepening sector penetration and driving sustainable revenue and portfolio growth. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong ability to identify and unlock opportunities within priority growth sectors and translate sector strategies into commercially viable, executable initiatives. The candidate will bring proven people leadership capability, sound commercial, financial, risk and governance judgement , and the ability to mobilise cross-functional stakeholders to deliver measurable commercial outcomes within approved risk appetite and regulatory frameworks . Essential Qualifications - NQF Level Professional Qualifications/Honour’s Degree Preferred Qualification Essential: Relevant undergraduate degree in commerce, finance, economics, business management, banking, sector development, or a related discipline. Preferred: Postgraduate qualification aligned to the role domain, client solutions, commercial strategy, business banking, or a related field. Minimum Experience Level Essential A minimum of 10 years’ experience in Commercial Banking, Business Banking or a closely related financial services environment . Demonstrated experience in developing and implementing commercial growth strategies. Proven experience in leading managers or senior commercial teams. Evidence of delivering measurable commercial outcomes through cross-functional stakeholders. Preferred 10–15+ years’ relevant experience in Commercial Banking, Business Banking or a comparable financial services environment. Extensive experience across multiple sectors, markets or client segments. A proven track record of delivering measurable market share growth, client acquisition, revenue growth or portfolio expansion. Senior leadership experience involving accountability for commercial performance and the execution of complex growth initiatives. Technical / Professional Knowledge Business Strategy Client Coverage Customer Value Proposition Communication Relationship Management Data governance and controls Stakeholder Engagement and Communication Skills Risk Appetite Sector Analysis Commercial Analysis Behavioural Competencies Strategic Influence Business Acumen Building Influential Partnerships Customer Focus Decision Making Driving for Results Establishing Customer Value Financial Acumen Disclaimer Preference will be given to candidates from the underrepresented groups Please contact the Nedbank Recruiting Team at +27 860 555 566 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Please contact the Nedbank Recruiting Team at +27 860 555 566",
